to the LORD: “For He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.” And the temple, the house of the LORD, was filled with a cloud","from":11},{"book":"2CH","chapter":29,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then Hezekiah said, “Now that you have consecrated yourselves to the LORD, come near and bring sacrifices and thank offerings to the house of the LORD.” So the assembly brought sacrifices and thank offerings, and all whose hearts were willing brought burnt offerings.","from":11},{"book":"ISA","chapter":51,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So the redeemed of the LORD will return and enter Zion with singing, crowned with everlasting joy. Gladness and joy will overtake them, and sorrow and sighing will flee.","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"14-18":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"words":[{"base":"H6666","lemma":"צְדָקָה","tr":"tse·da·qah","gloss":"righteousness","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":157},{"base":"H3772","lemma":"כָּרַת","tr":"ka·rat","gloss":"to cut: cut","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":288},{"base":"H1992","lemma":"הֵ֫מָּה","tr":"hem·mah","gloss":"they(masc.)","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":552},{"base":"H3063","lemma":"יְהוּדָה","tr":"ye·hu·dah","gloss":"Judah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":820},{"base":"H6780","lemma":"צֶ֫מַח","tr":"tse·mach","gloss":"branch","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1075},{"base":"H6779","lemma":"צָמַח","tr":"tsa·mach","gloss":"to spring","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":33},{"base":"H0983","lemma":"בֶּ֫טַח","tr":"be·tach","gloss":"security","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":42},{"base":"H6999","lemma":"קָטַר","tr":"qa·tar","gloss":"to offer: burn","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":116},{"base":"H6664","lemma":"צֶ֫דֶק","tr":"tse·deq","gloss":"righteousness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":119}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JER","chapter":23,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"In His days Judah will be saved, and Israel will dwell securely. And this is His name by which He will be called: The LORD Our Righteousness.","from":16},{"book":"HAG","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"For this is what the LORD of Hosts says: “Once more, in a little while, I will shake the heavens and the earth, the sea and the dry land.","from":14},{"book":"HAG","chapter":2,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"The latter glory of this house will be greater than the former, says the LORD of Hosts. And in this place I will provide peace, declares the LORD of Hosts.”","from":14},{"book":"JER","chapter":23,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Behold, the days are coming, declares the LORD, when I will raise up for David a righteous Branch, and He will reign wisely as King and will administer justice and righteousness in the land.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The scepter will not depart from Judah, nor the staff from between his feet, until Shiloh comes and the allegiance of the nations is his.","from":14},{"book":"ISA","chapter":4,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"On that day the Branch of the LORD will be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the land will be the pride and glory of Israelʼs survivors.","from":15},{"book":"ISA","chapter":11,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Then a shoot will spring up from the stump of Jesse, and a Branch from his roots will bear fruit.","from":15},{"book":"ISA","chapter":11,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Righteousness will be the belt around His hips, and faithfulness the sash around His waist.","from":15}],"notes":[{"id":"jer-23-5-branch","title":"A righteous Branch for David","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2}]},"19-26":{"people":[{"id":"jeremiah-h3414l","name":"Jeremiah","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":21},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2233","lemma":"זֶ֫רַע","tr":"ze·ra","gloss":"seed","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":229},{"base":"H1285","lemma":"בְּרִית","tr":"be·rit","gloss":"covenant","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":284},{"base":"H3915","lemma":"לַ֫יְלָה","tr":"lay·lah","gloss":"night","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":233},{"base":"H3119","lemma":"יוֹמָם","tr":"yo·mam","gloss":"by day","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":50},{"base":"H6565","lemma":"פָּרַר","tr":"pa·rar","gloss":"to break","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":50},{"base":"H3988","lemma":"מָאַס","tr":"ma·as","gloss":"to reject","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":76},{"base":"H5650","lemma":"עֶ֫בֶד","tr":"e·ved","gloss":"servant","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":800},{"base":"H8334","lemma":"שָׁרַת","tr":"sha·rat","gloss":"to minister","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":97},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1075},{"base":"H3414","lemma":"יִרְמְיָ֫הוּ","tr":"yir·me·yah","gloss":"Jeremiah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":147}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":74,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"The day is Yours, and also the night; You established the moon and the sun.","from":25},{"book":"PSA","chapter":74,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"You set all the boundaries of the earth; You made the summer and winter.","from":25},{"book":"JER","chapter":31,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Thus says the LORD, who gives the sun for light by day, who sets in order the moon and stars for light by night, who stirs up the sea so that its waves roar—the LORD of Hosts is His name:","from":25},{"book":"JER","chapter":31,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"“Only if this fixed order departed from My presence, declares the LORD, would Israelʼs descendants ever cease to be a nation before Me.”","from":25},{"book":"PSA","chapter":104,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"He made the moon to mark the seasons; the sun knows when to set.","from":25},{"book":"JER","chapter":31,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"This is what the LORD says: “Only if the heavens above could be measured and the foundations of the earth below searched out would I reject all of Israelʼs descendants because of all they have done,” declares the LORD.","from":26},{"book":"GEN","chapter":8,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"As long as the earth endures, seedtime and harvest, cold and heat, summer and winter, day and night shall never cease.”","from":20},{"book":"PSA","chapter":89,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"I will not violate My covenant or alter the utterance of My lips.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]}}